OL,3,AUS borrowing costs rise as attempts to
OL,4,Aease rates prove short-lived
OL,5,
OL,6,FLong-term borrowing costs in the US
OL,7,Frose again despite an announcement from
OL,8,Fthe government that it would intervene
OL,9,Fto try to lower them.
OL,11,FEarlier this week, the Treasury
OL,12,FDepartment said it would buy back more
OL,13,Fdebt in a bid to lower rates being
OL,14,Fcharged by investors on global bond
OL,15,Fmarkets, which governments and major
OL,16,Fcorporations rely on to borrow money.
OL,18,FWhile rates - or yields as they are
OL,19,Fcalled - eased on borrowing over 30
OL,20,Fyears following the intervention, they
OL,21,Fhave since risen again. Such moves can
OL,22,Faffect mortgage rates and car loans.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
